No CRITICAL error found in the component formulas. I found three GAPS and one MINOR in the as-built theorem/certification surface.

## Findings

### F-1 — GAP: the “ONE transport” is never constructed as one coherent object

> “there is ONE transport 𝕋 between the harness calculus … and the classifier/print calculus … with five clauses”

> “*Proof = the face table.* Each clause IS the cited composed theorem, at that theorem’s own grade and on its own perimeter”

The table proves five separately typed correspondences—division chains, polygon shears, residual-character formulas, algebra multiplication, and representative covariance. It neither defines a common domain/codomain for `𝕋` nor proves compatibility of those components. Citation of each face does not establish that the cited maps assemble into one transport.

There is also no uniqueness statement capable of supporting the emphatic “ONE.” For example, with \(E=2\), \(K=\mathbf F_5\), and the nontrivial character \(\eta(\nu)=(-1)^\nu\), replacing a gauge \(\widetilde E\) by \(\widetilde E\eta\) leaves its coboundary—and hence the M3 multiplication cocycle—unchanged while changing the gauge-level transport data. Thus M3 does not force the M2/M4 component.

If “ONE” means only “one organizational heading,” the remark says that; then it is not the theorem-level existential assertion displayed in WELD-M. Downstream may consume individual faces, but cross-face coherence is not licensed.

### F-2 — GAP: PE10’s claimed \(H^1=0\) uniqueness route is false

> “the DIRECT-H²/bar-resolution route proving Ẽ is THE canonical gauge — constructed from the cocycle alone and forced by H¹ = 0 uniqueness”

For the trivial coefficient action used by an ordinary twisted group algebra,
\[
H^1(C_E,K^\*)=\operatorname{Hom}(C_E,K^\*)=\mu_E(K),
\]
which is not generally zero.

Counter-configuration: \(E=2\), \(K=\mathbf F_5\). Then \(-1\in K^\*\) defines a nontrivial character \(\eta:C_2\to K^\*\). If \(\widetilde E\) is one gauge, then
\[
\partial(\widetilde E\eta)=\partial\widetilde E
\]
because \(\partial\eta=1\). Hence the gauge is not unique. Moreover, the displayed \(\widetilde E=E\circ\sigma\) is constructed from the pre-existing cochain \(E\) and chosen section \(\sigma\), not from the cocycle alone.

This does not refute WM-CLASS’s existence/class identity; it refutes the advertised decorrelated certification route and the word “canonical.”

### F-3 — MINOR: the final acceptance summary overstates WM-COB’s scope

> “WM-COB proved unconditional”

The theorem’s own clauses say otherwise:

> “(iii) … adds the [ILN]† VALUE LAW, scored stratum”

Only WM-COB(i), and the ε-kit field identity in (ii), are pair-unconditional. The composite identity involving \(c_{n+1}\) remains restricted to the scored stratum. On an off-stratum pair, \(D_j=\partial t_j\) remains licensed, but substitution of the cocycle value law does not.

The acceptance paragraph later says “at its displayed conditionality,” limiting the damage, so this is MINOR rather than a second theorem-level gap. Nevertheless, “WM-COB proved unconditional” cannot itself be used as a downstream scope grant.

### F-4 — GAP: the declared J-D consumption asks WM-FENCE for “freedom” it does not prove

> “the J-D block … consumes WM-FENCE’s (F-b)-freedom observation only through the already-adjudicated (J-D0) route”

WM-FENCE supplies character-triviality criteria:
\[
\operatorname{ord}(z_\mu)\mid A_\mu
\quad\text{or}\quad
\operatorname{ord}(z_\mu)\mid e_\mu A_\mu.
\]
It proves no freedom to vary \(z_\mu\), \(A_\mu\), the attained set, or the representative so that those divisibilities hold.

Counter-configuration: take \(K_\mu=\mathbf F_5\), \(z_\mu=2\) of order \(4\), \(A_\mu=1\), and an attained set containing \(1\). Absolute PERIM fails, and WM-FENCE provides no operation that can make it true. Any freedom or existence assertion must come independently from J-D0. The downstream design is explicitly “not executed,” so the present blast radius is nil, but the stated face-to-consumer interface is not licensed.

